  "sections": {
    "intro": {
      "label": "Overview",
      "heading": "White Dog Breeds",
      "html": "<p>White coats in dogs come from several genetic origins. Some breeds (like the Samoyed) carry a true white coat color. Others (like the West Highland White Terrier) have selectively bred white versions of normally varied breeds. Still others wear cream, ivory, or off-white coats that read as white in most lighting. What unites them is striking visual presence and the practical reality that white shows everything.</p><p>Owning a white dog means committing to coat maintenance — frequent baths, tear stain management around eyes, and tolerance for muddy paw prints turning into beige stains. The reward is one of the most photogenic dog types in existence. The breeds below are the most reliably white companions, from teacup-sized to mountain giants.</p>"
    },
    "care": {
      "label": "Breeds",
      "heading": "Top 10 White Dog Breeds",
      "html": "<style>@media (max-width:640px){.wf-breed-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr !important;}}</style><div class=\"wf-breed-grid\" style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;\"><div style=\"background:#ffffff;border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;\"><a href=\"/blogs/dog-breeds/samoyed\" class=\"wf-card-img\" style=\"display:block;\"><img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0554/5253/2790/files/01-adult-portrait_aa1c9c61-79c9-46a6-90f8-bfae44809d46.png?v=1777531208\" alt=\"Samoyed\" style=\"width:100%;aspect-ratio:3/2;height:auto;object-fit:cover;display:block;\"></a><div style=\"padding:16px;\"><h3 style=\"font-size:1em;font-weight:700;color:#1a1a1a;margin:0 0 8px 0;\">Samoyed</h3><div style=\"display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:10px;\"><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">Medium</span><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">High Energy</span><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">12–14 yrs lifespan</span></div><p style=\"font-size:0.85em;line-height:1.6;color:#6b7177;margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Samoyeds are the iconic pure-white breed — brilliant white double coats designed for arctic survival. Their slightly curled smile and white fluff make them among the most photographed dogs.</p><a href=\"/blogs/dog-breeds/samoyed\" style=\"font-size:0.8em;font-weight:600;color:#000000;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;\">Full guide →</a></div></div><div style=\"background:#ffffff;border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;\"><a href=\"/blogs/dog-breeds/west-highland-white-terrier\" class=\"wf-card-img\" style=\"display:block;\"><img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0554/5253/2790/files/01-adult-portrait_143b478b-9a62-4883-a821-a867f90fda52.png?v=1777532983\" alt=\"West Highland White Terrier\" style=\"width:100%;aspect-ratio:3/2;height:auto;object-fit:cover;display:block;\"></a><div style=\"padding:16px;\"><h3 style=\"font-size:1em;font-weight:700;color:#1a1a1a;margin:0 0 8px 0;\">West Highland White Terrier</h3><div style=\"display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:10px;\"><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">Small</span><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">Moderate Energy</span><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">12–16 yrs lifespan</span></div><p style=\"font-size:0.85em;line-height:1.6;color:#6b7177;margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Westies are compact white terriers with crisp double coats and bright, alert expressions. They are one of the most popular pure-white small breeds globally.</p><a href=\"/blogs/dog-breeds/west-highland-white-terrier\" style=\"font-size:0.8em;font-weight:600;color:#000000;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;\">Full guide →</a></div></div><div style=\"background:#ffffff;border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;\"><a href=\"/blogs/dog-breeds/maltese\" class=\"wf-card-img\" style=\"display:block;\"><img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0554/5253/2790/files/01-adult-portrait_52b2e29b-9970-4171-9914-f031bd1dbc39.png?v=1777529640\" alt=\"Maltese\" style=\"width:100%;aspect-ratio:3/2;height:auto;object-fit:cover;display:block;\"></a><div style=\"padding:16px;\"><h3 style=\"font-size:1em;font-weight:700;color:#1a1a1a;margin:0 0 8px 0;\">Maltese</h3><div style=\"display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:10px;\"><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">Small</span><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">Low Energy</span><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">12–15 yrs lifespan</span></div><p style=\"font-size:0.85em;line-height:1.6;color:#6b7177;margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Maltese dogs have pure white silky single coats. Their long flowing fur and bright dark eyes make them one of the most recognizable small white breeds in the world.</p><a href=\"/blogs/dog-breeds/maltese\" style=\"font-size:0.8em;font-weight:600;color:#000000;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;\">Full guide →</a></div></div><div style=\"background:#ffffff;border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;\"><a href=\"/blogs/dog-breeds/bichon-frise\" class=\"wf-card-img\" style=\"display:block;\"><img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0554/5253/2790/files/01-adult-portrait_f18b1943-860f-4cfb-8293-6c8f35589d8b.png?v=1777526057\" alt=\"Bichon Frise\" style=\"width:100%;aspect-ratio:3/2;height:auto;object-fit:cover;display:block;\"></a><div style=\"padding:16px;\"><h3 style=\"font-size:1em;font-weight:700;color:#1a1a1a;margin:0 0 8px 0;\">Bichon Frise</h3><div style=\"display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:10px;\"><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">Small</span><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">Low Energy</span><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">12–15 yrs lifespan</span></div><p style=\"font-size:0.85em;line-height:1.6;color:#6b7177;margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Bichons wear soft white curly coats trimmed into the iconic puffball shape. Their cloud-like appearance has made them popular companion dogs for centuries.</p><a href=\"/blogs/dog-breeds/bichon-frise\" style=\"font-size:0.8em;font-weight:600;color:#000000;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;\">Full guide →</a></div></div><div style=\"background:#ffffff;border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;\"><a href=\"/blogs/dog-breeds/great-pyrenees\" class=\"wf-card-img\" style=\"display:block;\"><img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0554/5253/2790/files/01-adult-portrait_fc60fab5-341d-4502-b606-b0f3110699a2.png?v=1777528307\" alt=\"Great Pyrenees\" style=\"width:100%;aspect-ratio:3/2;height:auto;object-fit:cover;display:block;\"></a><div style=\"padding:16px;\"><h3 style=\"font-size:1em;font-weight:700;color:#1a1a1a;margin:0 0 8px 0;\">Great Pyrenees</h3><div style=\"display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:10px;\"><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">Giant</span><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">Moderate Energy</span><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">10–12 yrs lifespan</span></div><p style=\"font-size:0.85em;line-height:1.6;color:#6b7177;margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Pyrs are massive mountain guardians with thick white double coats. Their size combined with pure white coloring gives them an unmistakable bear-like presence.</p><a href=\"/blogs/dog-breeds/great-pyrenees\" style=\"font-size:0.8em;font-weight:600;color:#000000;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;\">Full guide →</a></div></div><div style=\"background:#ffffff;border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;\"><a href=\"/blogs/dog-breeds/american-eskimo-dog\" class=\"wf-card-img\" style=\"display:block;\"><img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0554/5253/2790/files/01-adult-portrait_601d4f85-2e65-4ec8-8f55-5751a5a2ff18.png?v=1777572931\" alt=\"American Eskimo Dog\" style=\"width:100%;aspect-ratio:3/2;height:auto;object-fit:cover;display:block;\"></a><div style=\"padding:16px;\"><h3 style=\"font-size:1em;font-weight:700;color:#1a1a1a;margin:0 0 8px 0;\">American Eskimo Dog</h3><div style=\"display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:10px;\"><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">Small</span><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">High Energy</span><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">13–15 yrs lifespan</span></div><p style=\"font-size:0.85em;line-height:1.6;color:#6b7177;margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Eskies come in toy, miniature, and standard sizes — all wearing brilliant white double coats. They look like miniature versions of arctic working breeds.</p><a href=\"/blogs/dog-breeds/american-eskimo-dog\" style=\"font-size:0.8em;font-weight:600;color:#000000;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;\">Full guide →</a></div></div><div style=\"background:#ffffff;border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;\"><a href=\"/blogs/dog-breeds/coton-de-tulear\" class=\"wf-card-img\" style=\"display:block;\"><img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0554/5253/2790/files/01-adult-portrait_09b5558c-3c7a-4e4c-9117-88ff56e9cda4.png?v=1777580472\" alt=\"Coton de Tulear\" style=\"width:100%;aspect-ratio:3/2;height:auto;object-fit:cover;display:block;\"></a><div style=\"padding:16px;\"><h3 style=\"font-size:1em;font-weight:700;color:#1a1a1a;margin:0 0 8px 0;\">Coton de Tulear</h3><div style=\"display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:10px;\"><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">Toy</span><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">High Energy</span><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">15–19 yrs lifespan</span></div><p style=\"font-size:0.85em;line-height:1.6;color:#6b7177;margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Cotons are small Madagascan companion dogs with cotton-soft white coats. Their name literally means cotton from Tulear, referring to their distinctive coat texture.</p><a href=\"/blogs/dog-breeds/coton-de-tulear\" style=\"font-size:0.8em;font-weight:600;color:#000000;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;\">Full guide →</a></div></div><div style=\"background:#ffffff;border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;\"><a href=\"/blogs/dog-breeds/komondor\" class=\"wf-card-img\" style=\"display:block;\"><img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0554/5253/2790/files/01-adult-portrait_1f47fc11-2a4f-4a15-b30f-57b5ccc4d267.png?v=1777575401\" alt=\"Komondor\" style=\"width:100%;aspect-ratio:3/2;height:auto;object-fit:cover;display:block;\"></a><div style=\"padding:16px;\"><h3 style=\"font-size:1em;font-weight:700;color:#1a1a1a;margin:0 0 8px 0;\">Komondor</h3><div style=\"display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:10px;\"><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">Large</span><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">High Energy</span><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">10–12 yrs lifespan</span></div><p style=\"font-size:0.85em;line-height:1.6;color:#6b7177;margin:0 0 12px 0;\">The Komondor is a Hungarian livestock guardian instantly recognizable for its white corded coat that resembles dreadlocks. The unique coat develops naturally as the puppy grows.</p><a href=\"/blogs/dog-breeds/komondor\" style=\"font-size:0.8em;font-weight:600;color:#000000;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;\">Full guide →</a></div></div><div style=\"background:#ffffff;border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;\"><a href=\"/blogs/dog-breeds/standard-poodle\" class=\"wf-card-img\" style=\"display:block;\"><img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0554/5253/2790/files/01-adult-portrait_e07879b9-c778-416b-b2d0-675e3d174f57.png?v=1777531939\" alt=\"Standard Poodle\" style=\"width:100%;aspect-ratio:3/2;height:auto;object-fit:cover;display:block;\"></a><div style=\"padding:16px;\"><h3 style=\"font-size:1em;font-weight:700;color:#1a1a1a;margin:0 0 8px 0;\">Standard Poodle</h3><div style=\"display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:10px;\"><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">Large</span><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">High Energy</span><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">10–18 yrs lifespan</span></div><p style=\"font-size:0.85em;line-height:1.6;color:#6b7177;margin:0 0 12px 0;\">White Standard Poodles wear the breed's iconic curly single-layer coat in pure white. The combination of elegance and brightness makes white Poodles among the most striking show dogs.</p><a href=\"/blogs/dog-breeds/standard-poodle\" style=\"font-size:0.8em;font-weight:600;color:#000000;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;\">Full guide →</a></div></div><div style=\"background:#ffffff;border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;\"><a href=\"/blogs/dog-breeds/pomeranian\" class=\"wf-card-img\" style=\"display:block;\"><img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0554/5253/2790/files/01-adult-portrait_f6ec91b8-a841-4577-8a34-154f13d44251.png?v=1777530441\" alt=\"Pomeranian\" style=\"width:100%;aspect-ratio:3/2;height:auto;object-fit:cover;display:block;\"></a><div style=\"padding:16px;\"><h3 style=\"font-size:1em;font-weight:700;color:#1a1a1a;margin:0 0 8px 0;\">Pomeranian</h3><div style=\"display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:10px;\"><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">Toy</span><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">Moderate Energy</span><span style=\"font-family:'figmaMono','SF Mono',monospace;font-size:0.65em;background:#f0f0f0;border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;color:#555;\">12–16 yrs lifespan</span></div><p style=\"font-size:0.85em;line-height:1.6;color:#6b7177;margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Pomeranians come in many colors but white is among the most striking — a tiny five-pound cloud of brilliant white fluff that draws attention everywhere.</p><a href=\"/blogs/dog-breeds/pomeranian\" style=\"font-size:0.8em;font-weight:600;color:#000000;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;\">Full guide →</a></div></div></div>"
    },
    "special": {
      "label": "Considerations",
      "heading": "Keeping White Coats White",
      "html": "<p>White coats stain easily — tear stains, food drips, grass marks, and muddy paws all show up dramatically. Owners of white dogs need to commit to weekly bathing or at least a thorough wipe-down, daily face cleaning around eyes and mouth, and immediate post-walk paw rinses. Tear stain remover products and waterless dog shampoos are common essentials in white-dog households.</p><p>Many white-coated breeds are also prone to skin sensitivity and sunburn. Pink-pigmented noses and bellies can sunburn during outdoor activity, requiring dog-safe sunscreen. White breeds also show skin irritations more visibly than dark-coated dogs, which is actually an advantage — issues are caught and treated faster.</p>\n<!-- WOOFFY_INTERNAL_LINKS_v1 -->\n<section class=\"related-reading\">\n<h2>Related Reading</h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://thewooffy.com/blogs/dog-breeds/komondor\">Komondor</a></li><li><a href=\"https://thewooffy.com/blogs/dog-breeds/pomeranian\">Pomeranian</a></li><li><a href=\"https://thewooffy.com/blogs/dog-breeds/standard-poodle\">Standard Poodle</a></li><li><a href=\"https://thewooffy.com/blogs/dog-breeds/japanese-dog-breeds\">Japanese Dog Breeds</a></li><li><a href=\"https://thewooffy.com/blogs/dog-breeds/best-dogs-for-hot-climates\">Best Dogs for Hot Climates</a></li></ul>\n</section>"
    }
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "What is the most popular white dog breed?",
      "a": "The Maltese, West Highland White Terrier, and Bichon Frise are among the most popular pure-white companion breeds globally. The Samoyed and Great Pyrenees are the most popular larger white breeds."
    },
    {
      "q": "Do white dogs need more grooming?",
      "a": "They need more cleaning, not necessarily more grooming. White coats show stains and dirt more visibly, requiring more frequent baths, tear stain management, and post-walk wipe-downs. The actual brushing and trimming requirements depend on the breed's coat type."
    },
    {
      "q": "Are white dogs prone to deafness?",
      "a": "Some are, particularly when white coloring comes from extreme piebald or albino genetics. White Boxers, Dalmatians, and white Bull Terriers have higher congenital deafness rates than their colored counterparts. Most pure-white breeds (Samoyed, Maltese, Bichon, Westie) do not share this risk."
    },
    {
      "q": "Do white dog breeds tear stain?",
      "a": "Yes, particularly small white breeds like Maltese, Bichons, and Westies. Tear stains are reddish-brown marks under the eyes caused by porphyrin in tears. Daily face wiping with a damp cloth and tear stain removers help manage the appearance."
    }
  ]
}